    Wire the projection reduction core into the production diagnostic path
    
    The production diagnostic test rebuilds the registered model commitment from
    the saved private table randomness, verifies the real gpt2-seq16 trace, takes
    the verified activation and output rows of the layer-0 key projection
    consumer, and recomputes the raw accumulator from the trusted weight rows and
    the verified activation. It then arranges the real weight rows in the hidden
    session's table layout and runs the production diagnostic hidden LIN prover
    and verifier on that table, with the projection reduction core checked against
    the same values. Changed output, changed coefficients and a changed table
    identity are rejected by the same session.
    
    This is the diagnostic transition only: it keeps every existing full-weight
    relation check, adds no protocol object or message, and does not claim the
    hidden-input consumer closure.

